.\" Manual page for blepo
.TH BLEPO 1 "August 2026" "blepo 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blepo \- watch YouTube channels without ads, distractions, or tracking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blepo
.br
.B blepo add
.I CHANNEL
.br
.B blepo
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blepo
fetches recent videos from configured YouTube channels, removes Shorts and
videos already marked as watched, and presents the remaining videos as a
numbered list.
Selected videos are played through
.BR mpv (1).
Blepo stores watched video IDs locally and requires no YouTube account or API
key.
.PP
When YouTube RSS is unavailable, Blepo uses
.BR yt-dlp (1)
as a fallback.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B blepo
Fetch recent unwatched videos and open the interactive selection prompt.
.TP
.BI "blepo add " CHANNEL
Resolve a YouTube channel and add it to the configuration file. Existing
settings, comments, and channels are preserved. Adding the same canonical
channel more than once is rejected.
.TP
.BR "blepo \-h" ", " "blepo \-\-help" ", " "blepo help"
Display command usage and examples.
.SH ADDING A CHANNEL
The
.B add
command accepts any of the following forms:
.TP
.B @Fireship
A YouTube handle.
.TP
.B https://www.youtube.com/@Fireship
A YouTube channel URL. Legacy
.B /channel/
and
.B /user/
channel URLs are also accepted.
.TP
.B UCsBjURrPoezykLs9EqgamOA
A canonical YouTube channel ID beginning with
.BR UC .
.PP
For example:
.PP
.nf
blepo add @Fireship
.fi
.PP
Blepo asks
.BR yt-dlp (1)
for the canonical channel name and ID, validates them, and writes an entry like
this:
.PP
.nf
[[channels]]
name = "Fireship"
id = "UCsBjURrPoezykLs9EqgamOA"
.fi
.PP
This removes the need to find or copy the internal
.B UC
identifier manually.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
After
.B blepo
displays the numbered video list, the prompt accepts:
.TP
.I number
Play the selected video and mark it as watched.
.TP
.BI w number
Mark one video as watched without playing it. For example,
.B w3
marks video 3.
.TP
.B wa
Mark every currently displayed video as watched. This affects only the videos
fetched within the configured time window, not the complete history of each
channel.
.TP
.B q
Quit without selecting another video. Pressing Enter on an empty prompt also
quits.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration uses TOML. The optional
.B fetch_window_days
setting controls how far Blepo looks back and defaults to 7 days.
.PP
.nf
fetch_window_days = 7

[[channels]]
name = "3Blue1Brown"
id = "UCYO_jab_esuFRV4b17AJtAw"
.fi
.PP
Manual editing remains supported, although
.B blepo add
is the recommended way to add channels.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/blepo/config.toml
Configuration file on Linux.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/blepo/config.toml
Configuration file on macOS.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/blepo/watched.json
Watched-video state on Linux.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/blepo/watched.json
Watched-video state on macOS.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.BR mpv (1)
Plays selected videos.
.TP
.BR yt-dlp (1)
Resolves channel metadata, retrieves fallback video listings, and resolves
YouTube streams for mpv.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Blepo exits with status 0 after a successful command or normal interactive
quit. It exits with a non-zero status when configuration, channel resolution,
storage, or playback setup fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add a channel by handle:
.PP
.nf
blepo add @Fireship
.fi
.PP
Add a channel by URL:
.PP
.nf
blepo add https://www.youtube.com/@Fireship
.fi
.PP
Fetch videos and start the interactive prompt:
.PP
.nf
blepo
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR yt-dlp (1)
